// A cell whose lower bounds its conjuncts refuse is reported as
// "unsatisfiable constraints" over the conjuncts alone.
//
// Run: /home/eric/tmp/review-2026-11-16/bin/graphix --no-cache --check \
//        design/review-2026-11-16/repro/t-tvar-b-unsatisfiable-names-no-lower-bound.gx
//
// Expected: a refusal that says what conflicts: the payload of `b` holds an
//   i64 (`B(1)`) and an f64 (`b <- B(1.5)`), and `b.0 + b.0` needs one
//   numeric type.
// Observed:
//     at: line 19, column 9 .. in: B(1)
//     unsatisfiable constraints on '_NNNN: Number & Singleton
//   `Number & Singleton` is satisfiable (i64 meets it); the two types built
//   into the payload, which the conjuncts refuse together, are not named,
//   nor is the operator or the write. The same text answers
//   `add(b.0, b.0)` over `let add = |x, y| x + y` and a `'a: OneNumber`
//   parameter.
type B<'p> = Abstract<'p>;
let b = B(1);
let r = b.0 + b.0;
b <- B(1.5);
r
